        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 rounded-2xl p-8 text-gray-200">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            Peeling is a film problem. It means a coating was asked to stick to wood that was wet, dirty, glazed or already coated, or that a penetrating product was applied so heavily it became a film. The fix is never another coat on top; it is a full strip, a brightener, real drying time and a sprinkle test before anything new goes on.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0">
            Once the deck is clean and absorbent, the choice is simple. If you want it to look like wood and never peel again, use a thin penetrating oil and recoat it on schedule. If you want a solid colour, accept that you are painting a floor and prep accordingly every single time.
          </p>
        </div>

